From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:30:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(model): Ollama's served window on any host and at runtime

Patch 0054 made the context probe report the window Ollama serves, but only for a local address, and the runtime num_ctx still came from the model's trained maximum. An Ollama behind a DNS name or a reverse proxy got the GGUF maximum from /api/show (131072 for llama3.2:3b where the server serves 65536), and a cached maximum on such a host was never checked again. At runtime query_ollama_num_ctx returned the Modelfile num_ctx else the maximum, which Hermes sent as options.num_ctx (Ollama's /v1 ignores it) and which lifted the window the minimum-context check saw past what Ollama truncates at.

A self-hosted server is now one the probe waterfall recognizes on any host, not only a local address; for Ollama every path (custom endpoint probe, /api/show step, cache reconcile, runtime num_ctx) uses the served window: /api/ps context_length, else num_ctx, else what a load gives (OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH), else 4096 with a warning. The load waits up to 180 s, so a large model is not taken for 4096. num_ctx is no longer kept on disk, so an older build's stored maximum is not read back. model.context_length wins: it becomes num_ctx with no probe, and the compressor clamp cannot undercut it. Hosted Ollama (ollama.com) keeps the model maximum.
